#
# Counter-example for math:IngestSourceHeldConstraint: a math:IngestRun whose
# math:parseSource witness HOLDS NOTHING — it carries neither math:retainedSource
# (verbatim) nor math:sourceDigest (by reference), so the put leg has no complement
# to project along and the source is unrecoverable. That is the graph-side residue of
# the front-end's math:UnreadableIngestSource refusal, one step later.
#
# Deliberately a BARE math:IngestRun rather than one of the three concrete bridge
# subclasses: the dialect-specific retention constraints are scoped to math:RIngestRun /
# math:ProofIngestRun / math:ONNXIngestRun, so the abstract unifier isolates the shared
# hold-your-source rule alone. The run is well-formed everywhere else — it carries the
# full grounding frame (so it is not math:UngroundedIngestRun) and it DID produce a
# structured codomain (so the native math:UnliftableIngest gate stays quiet). It fires
# math:IngestSourceHeldConstraint (shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent →
# math:UnreadableIngestSource).
@prefix math:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix ex:    <http://example.org/math/ingest-source-held-neither/> .

ex:run a math:IngestRun ;
    math:parseSource ex:srcWitness ;
    logic:instantiatesSchema ex:schema ;
    logic:instantiatesPlan ex:plan ;
    math:ingestCorrespondence ex:corr .

# The amnesic witness: load-bearing, and holding neither form of its source.
ex:srcWitness a math:MathematicalObject ; logic:loadBearing true .

ex:schema a logic:ActionSchema .
ex:plan a logic:Plan .
ex:corr a logic:Correspondence ;
    logic:morphismClass logic:LossyLens ;
    logic:mnemomorphic true .

# The lift DID produce a codomain, so the produced-nothing native gate is not in play.
ex:lifted a math:MathematicalObject ; gmeow:wasGeneratedBy ex:run .
